### 7 – Frontend: Admin Page (`curriculum_lessons/Index.vue`)

#### [NEW] `resources/js/Pages/myclass2026/roles/school-admin/weekly_system/curriculum_lessons/Index.vue`

**Role:** School Admin. Manages book structure, controls editing locks, and tracks teacher submissions.

**Two-section layout (tabs or stepper):**

**Section A — Manage Curricula & Locks**
- `q-form` with:
  - `q-input` → Curriculum Name (required)
  - `q-input type="textarea"` → Description (optional)
  - `q-select` → Grade (loaded from existing API)
  - `q-select` → Subject (loaded from existing API)
  - `q-date` picker → **Edit Lock Date** (optional) — admin picks the deadline after which nobody can edit plans
  - School auto-read from `$page.props.auth.user.school_id`
- Existing curricula list (`q-table`) shows the lock date with a `q-chip`:
  - 🟡 Upcoming lock: "Locks on [date]"
  - 🔴 Locked: "Locked since [date]" (all plans under it are read-only)
- Admin can **edit the lock date** at any time (inline edit to enable/disable editing)
- Submit POST → `/weekly-system/api/curriculum`
- 422 error → shows `q-banner color="negative"` inline (never a popup)

**Section B — Tracking (Who did / didn't do)**
- Admin selects a curriculum → backend calls `progress()` which:
  - Gets **all teachers in the school** (from `teachers` table where `school_id` matches)
  - Checks which of them have submitted plans (i.e. have a row in `curriculum_lesson_plans` for this curriculum)
  - Returns two lists: ✅ teachers who submitted, ❌ teachers who haven't
- UI shows a `q-table` split into two sections or with a filter toggle
- Columns: Teacher Name, Subject, Grade, # Plans Submitted, Last Updated

---

### 8 – Frontend: Teacher Page (`curriculum_lessons/Index.vue`)

#### [NEW] `resources/js/Pages/myclass2026/roles/teacher/weekly_system/curriculum_lessons/Index.vue`

**Role:** Teacher. Selects a curriculum and creates lesson plans.

**Two-section layout:**

**Section A — Select Curriculum**
- Loads curricula filtered by **teacher's assigned subjects + grades** (via CST / schedule assignments)
- Calls `GET /api/curriculum?teacher_id=me` — backend joins through CST records
- Read-only view showing curriculum name, description, lock date with countdown chip:
  - 🟢 Open — no lock set
  - ⏳ "3 days left to edit" — lock is approaching
  - 🔴 "Locked since [date]" — no editing allowed

**Section B — My Lesson Plans** (appears when a curriculum is selected)
- `q-table` showing **only this teacher’s plans** for the selected curriculum.
- Status badge per row: `q-chip` colored by status (draft=grey, active=green, completed=blue).
- Edit/delete buttons per row: **disabled with a lock icon** when `status !== 0` OR today >= curriculum's `edit_lock_date`.
- "Add Plan" button → opens `q-dialog` with a lean form (title, cw, hw, objectives, planned_date).
  - Button hidden/disabled if curriculum is date-locked.
- **Lock is enforced on the server too** — backend returns 403 for edit/delete on locked plans.

**Quasar Import (project standard):**
```js
import { useQuasar } from 'quasar'
const $q = useQuasar()
// All q-* components auto-registered globally via app.js — no individual imports needed
```

